  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Motzi, Matzah:1": {
   "kind": "heading",
   "en": "Motzi, Matzah"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Motzi, Matzah:2": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "Take the matzot in the order they were placed: the broken piece between the two whole ones. Hold all three in your hand. Recite 'Hamotzi' with intent on the top matzah, and 'Al Achilat Matzah' with intent on the broken one. Then break off an olive-sized piece from the top whole matzah and a second olive-sized piece from the broken one. Dip them in salt and eat the two pieces while reclining."
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Motzi, Matzah:3": {
   "kind": "prayer",
   "node": "meal.hamotzi"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Motzi, Matzah:4": {
   "kind": "prayer",
   "node": "brachot.mitzvot"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Maror:1": {
   "kind": "heading",
   "en": "Maror"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Maror:2": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "Each person at the table takes an olive-sized piece of maror, dips it in charoset, shakes off the excess charoset, recites the blessing, and eats it without reclining."
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Maror:3": {
   "kind": "prayer"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Korech:1": {
   "kind": "heading",
   "en": "Korech"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Korech:2": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "Each person at the table takes an olive-bulk of the third matzah and an olive-bulk of maror, wraps them together, and eats them while reclining, without a blessing. Before eating, one says:"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Korech:3": {
   "kind": "note",
   "en": "In remembrance of the Temple, as Hillel did. Hillel used to wrap matzah and maror together and eat them, to fulfill the verse: 'With matzah and bitter herbs they shall eat it.'"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Tzafun:1": {
   "kind": "heading",
   "en": "Tzafun"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Tzafun:2": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "After the meal, each person takes an olive-sized piece of the hidden matzah (the Afikoman) and eats it while reclining. It must be eaten before midnight."
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:1": {
   "kind": "heading",
   "en": "Blessing"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:2": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "We pour the third cup and recite Birkat HaMazon."
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:3": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "Before Birkat HaMazon, we say:"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:4": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "<small><small><small><b>שִׁיר</b> הַמַּעֲלוֹת בְּשׁוּב יְהֹוָה אֶת שִׁיבַת צִיּוֹן הָיִינוּ כְּחֹלְמִים: אָז יִמָּלֵא שְׂחוֹק פִּינוּ וּלְשׁוֹנֵנוּ רִנָּה אָז יֹאמְרוּ בַגּוֹיִם הִגְדִּיל יְהֹוָה לַעֲשׂוֹת עִם אֵלֶּה: הִגְדִּיל יְהֹוָה לַעֲשׂוֹת עִמָּנוּ הָיִינוּ שְׂמֵחִים: שׁוּבָה יְהֹוָה אֶת <small>(שבותנו)</small>",
     "kind": "prayer",
     "node": "birkat_hamazon.shir_hamaalot"
    },
    {
     "text": " שְׁבִיתֵנוּ כַּאֲפִיקִים בַּנֶּגֶב: הַזֹּרְעִים בְּדִמְעָה בְּרִנָּה יִקְצֹרוּ: הָלוֹךְ יֵלֵךְ וּבָכֹה נֹשֵׂא מֶשֶׁךְ הַזָּרַע בֹּא יָבוֹא בְרִנָּה נֹשֵׂא אֲלֻמֹּתָיו:</small></small> </small>",
     "kind": "prayer",
     "node": "birkat_hamazon.shir_hamaalot"
    }
   ]
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:5": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "Mayim Acharonim (washing hands after the meal) is obligatory before Birkat HaMazon. Do not interrupt between the washing and the blessing, even with Torah study. Place your tallit on your head while reciting Birkat HaMazon, in accordance with 'Prepare yourselves to meet your God, O Israel.' When lifting the cup to bless, it is customary to say:"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:6": {
   "kind": "prayer"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:7": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "Three who ate together are obligated in Zimun. The Zimun is as follows:"
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:8": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "<small><small><b>המזמן אומר:</b></small>",
     "kind": "speaker",
     "en": "The one who invites says:"
    },
    {
     "text": " <b>רַבּוֹתַי.</b> מִיר וֶועלֶן בֶּענְטְשְׁן ",
     "kind": "prayer",
     "role": "chazzan"
    },
    {
     "text": "<small>(אוֹ רַבּוֹתַי נְבָרֵךְ)</small>",
     "kind": "prayer",
     "role": "chazzan",
     "en": "(Or: Friends, let us bless)"
    },
    {
     "text": ":</small>",
     "kind": "prayer",
     "role": "chazzan"
    }
   ]
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:9": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "<small><small><b>המסובים עונים:</b></small>",
     "kind": "speaker",
     "en": "The guests answer:"
    },
    {
     "text": " <b>יְהִי</b> שֵׁם יְהֹוָה מְבֹרָךְ מֵעַתָּה וְעַד עוֹלָם:</small>",
     "kind": "prayer",
     "role": "congregation"
    }
   ]
  },
  "he:Pesach Haggadah/Barech:10": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "<small><small><b>המזמן אומר:</b></small>",
     "kind": "speaker",
     "en": "The one who invites says:"
